# <%= current_page.data.title %>

This section covers production-only concerns. Complete [Starting a new component](../new-component/) first to get your application running in a non-production environment, then come back here before going live.

Work through it in this order:

1. [Productionise your application](productionise-your-application.html) — get approved for production, prepare your production configuration, and understand what happens before, during and after a deployment.
2. [Health probes](health-endpoints.html) — configure the readiness and liveness checks the platform uses to keep your application available.
3. [Monitoring](monitoring.html) — make sure you can see what your application is doing in production.
4. [Alerting](alerting.html) — make sure the right people find out when something goes wrong.
5. [Operational Acceptance Testing](oat.html) — check whether your release needs an OAT and how to prepare for one.
6. [Shuttering](shutter.html) — set up and test a shutter page for user-facing services.

There may be other business processes you need to go through, but they are out of scope of this section.
